window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"work-with-files\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">处理文件</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>当任务需要生成文件时，请向 ChatGPT 提供源数据、预期的文件类型、 结构，以及对该任务而言重要的审查标准。可用的预览和审查工具 取决于你所使用的界面。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E3dDr_QtBuo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：在 ChatGPT 中处理文档、电子表格和演示文稿（需联网）</a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用会在聊天旁边预览生成的文档、演示文稿、 电子表格和 PDF 文件。启用自动预览后，应用可以在任务完成时 打开生成的文件。</p> <p>如果 HTML 预览可用，生成的 <code>.html</code> 和 <code>.htm</code> 文件也可以 作为交互式预览打开。你可以在渲染后的预览与源代码视图之间切换，以检查 输出结果或其底层 HTML。</p> <p>打开独立的 <code>.tex</code> 文件，即可一边编辑 LaTeX 源码，一边查看 PDF 预览。内置编译器可用时，应用会编译文档，并在编辑后刷新预览。如果编译失败，最后一次成功生成的 PDF 仍会显示，你对源码的修改也会保留。</p> <p>使用批注指向受支持预览中的某个具体部分，并请求有针对性的修改。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在网页版 ChatGPT Work 中，可以附加源文件，或让 ChatGPT 创建 文档、演示文稿、电子表格或 PDF。在聊天中检查生成的文件， 需要时将其下载，并针对下一版本提供具体反馈。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI 可以在工作目录中创建和编辑文件，但不包含 可视化文件预览或批注界面。请让 Codex 报告每个输出路径，以及 它所运行的检查。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>IDE 扩展可以在工作区中创建和编辑文件。请在编辑器中审查文本文件和 代码文件，并用兼容的查看器打开文档、演示文稿、电子表格或 PDF 文件。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用正在显示生成的演示文稿预览</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"create-files-for-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">创建文件以供审查</h2> <p>对于电子表格和演示文稿，请说明你希望包含的工作表、列、图表、 幻灯片章节和检查项。请让 ChatGPT 解释它将输出保存在哪里， 以及如何检查了结果。</p> <p><a id=\"refine-files-with-annotations\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"review-and-refine-files\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"_3\">使用批注完善文件</h2> <p>批注让你可以指向文件中的某个具体部分，并告诉 ChatGPT 要修改什么。用于代码、Markdown 文件和网站的同一套批注工作流， 也同样适用于文档、电子表格和演示文稿。</p> <p>例如，你可以：</p> <ul> <li>选中网站上的导航栏，让 ChatGPT 更改其字体。</li> <li>高亮投资论点中的一项主张，并要求提供来源。</li> <li>标记幻灯片上的图表，并要求给出更清晰的标签。</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT 会把所选区域作为请求的上下文，因此你无需从头开始， 也不必改动已经满意的部分，就能完善文件。批注在初稿完成后尤其有用， 因为此时工作通常需要审查和迭代。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"review-and-refine-files-on-the-web\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">在网页上审查和完善文件</h2> <p>打开或下载生成的文件，并在合适的查看器中检查。请求修改时， 请指明需要处理的页面、幻灯片、工作表、表格或段落，并说明哪些内容 应保持不变。在下载下一版本前，请让 ChatGPT 报告新的文件名以及 它所执行的检查。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"_5\">审查和完善文件</h2> <p>任务运行时，可以使用聊天侧边栏。它可以显示智能体的计划、 来源、生成的文件和聊天摘要，便于你引导工作、 检查生成的文件并要求再处理一轮。</p> <p>请让 ChatGPT 说明每个文件保存在哪里，以及如何验证了 结果。使用预览检查输出，然后针对需要再次处理的 结构、数据、布局或验证给出具体反馈。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"work-with-files\">Work with files</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>When a task produces a file, give ChatGPT the source data, expected file type, structure, and review criteria that matter for the task. The preview and review tools depend on the surface you use.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E3dDr_QtBuo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Work with documents, spreadsheets, and presentations in ChatGPT (online)</a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app previews generated documents, presentations, spreadsheets, and PDF files alongside the chat. When automatic previews are enabled, the app can open a generated file after a task finishes.</p> <p>When HTML previews are available, generated <code>.html</code> and <code>.htm</code> files can also open as interactive previews. Switch between the rendered preview and source view to inspect the output or its underlying HTML.</p> <p>Open a standalone <code>.tex</code> file to edit its LaTeX source alongside a PDF preview. When the built-in compiler is available, the app compiles the document and refreshes the preview after edits. If compilation fails, the last successful PDF remains visible and your source edits are preserved.</p> <p>Use annotations to point at a specific part of a supported preview and request a focused revision.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT Work on the web, attach source files or ask ChatGPT to create a document, presentation, spreadsheet, or PDF. Review the generated file in the chat, download it when needed, and give targeted feedback for the next version.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex CLI can create and edit files in the working directory, but it doesn't include a visual file preview or annotation interface. Ask Codex to report each output path and the checks it ran.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The IDE extension can create and edit files in the workspace. Review text and code files in the editor, and open documents, presentations, spreadsheets, or PDF files in a compatible viewer.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app showing a generated presentation preview</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"create-files-for-review\">Create files for review</h2> <p>For spreadsheets and presentations, describe the sheets, columns, charts, slide sections, and checks you expect. Ask ChatGPT to explain where it saved the output and how it checked the result.</p> <p><a id=\"refine-files-with-annotations\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"review-and-refine-files\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"refine-files-with-annotations\">Refine files with annotations</h2> <p>Annotations let you point to a specific part of a file and tell ChatGPT what to change. The same annotation workflow available for code, Markdown files, and websites also works with documents, spreadsheets, and presentations.</p> <p>For example, you can:</p> <ul> <li>Select a navigation bar on a website and ask ChatGPT to change its font.</li> <li>Highlight a claim in an investment thesis and ask for its source.</li> <li>Mark a chart on a slide and request a clearer label.</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT uses the selected area as context for your request, so you can refine the file without starting over or changing the parts you already like. Annotations are particularly useful after the first draft, when the work needs review and iteration.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"review-and-refine-files-on-the-web\">Review and refine files on the web</h2> <p>Open or download the generated file to review it in the appropriate viewer. When you request a revision, name the page, slide, sheet, table, or passage that needs attention and describe what should stay unchanged. Ask ChatGPT to report the new file name and the checks it performed before you download the next version.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"review-and-refine-files\">Review and refine files</h2> <p>Use the chat sidebar while a task runs. It can surface the agent's plan, sources, generated files, and chat summary so you can steer the work, inspect generated files, and request another pass.</p> <p>Ask ChatGPT to explain where it saved each file and how it verified the result. Use the preview to inspect the output, then give focused feedback about the structure, data, layout, or validation that needs another pass.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation</a></li> </ul>"};
